.TH BLOCKFORGE 1 "" "BlockForge" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
blockforge \- a fast, modern Minecraft launcher
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B blockforge
[\fB\-\-debug\fR] [\fB\-\-debug\-level\fR \fIN\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B blockforge
installs and starts Minecraft: Java Edition. Without a command it opens the launcher window.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B gui
Open the launcher window (the default).
.TP
.B list
List instances.
.TP
.B create \fINAME\fR
Create an instance.
.TP
.B launch \fIINSTANCE\fR
Start an instance.
.TP
.B account
Show accounts, add an offline one, or sign in with Microsoft.
.TP
.B search \fIQUERY\fR
Search Modrinth.
.TP
.B import \fISOURCE\fR
Create an instance from a Modrinth modpack (a .mrpack file or a project id).
.TP
.B java
Show the Javas found on this computer.
.TP
.B paths
Show where the data lives.
.PP
Run
.B blockforge \-\-help
or
.B blockforge \fICOMMAND\fR \-\-help
for all commands and options.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BLOCKFORGE_DIR
Keep the launcher's files in this folder instead of
.IR ~/.local/share/blockforge .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/blockforge
Instances, accounts, settings and downloaded game files.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/riyadmondol2006/BlockForge
